  DIFF q m1-ord-n03.teach: fixture undefined | PK [{"h":"The idea","list":["Half-life (t½) and the rate constant k are two ways of stating the same first-order decline: t½ = {{frac:0.693|k}}.","The relation has no concentration term, so the half-life does not change as the solution decomposes, and one half-life describes the drug at all doses.","A half-life is a time; reciprocal time belongs to k."]},{"h":"Where to read more","t":"Introduction.pdf, slide 19."}]
  DIFF q m1-ord-n03.teachImg: fixture undefined | PK "slide_Introduction_p22"
  DIFF q m1-ord-n03.quote: fixture undefined | PK "this is one that I want you to know. So that will not be on your equation sheet. This is the one that you take to your grave with you, OK? 0.693 over K."
  DIFF q m2-n-cl2.prof: fixture "Professor" | PK "Mosley"
  DIFF q m2-n-cl2.steps.1.why: fixture "Total body clearance is k multiplied by VD, and neither is given directly: the stem gives a half-life and a percentage. Naming the relation first shows which two quantities have to be built. The professor leaves this relation off the exam equation sheet, so it has to be known." | PK "Total body clearance is k multiplied by VD, and neither is given directly: the stem gives a half-life and a percentage. Naming the relation first shows which two quantities have to be built. Dr. Mosley leaves this relation off the exam equation sheet, so it has to be known."
