  DIFF q inf-n1.teach: fixture undefined | PK [{"h":"The idea","list":["Steady state is where first-order removal matches the fixed input, so Css (steady-state concentration) = {{frac:R|Cl}}, with R the infusion rate.","When clearance is not given, it is built from the half-life and the volume of distribution: Cl = k × VD, with k = {{frac:0.693|t½}}.","Once those two constants are found, the calculation is one division."]},{"h":"Where to read more","t":"3IntravenousInfusions.pdf, slide \"Example 1\"."}]
