  DIFF q m5-n07.teach: fixture undefined | PK [{"h":"The idea","list":["When an oral problem is given as an equation, tmax (the time to peak) = {{frac:ln(ka/k)|ka - k}} needs nothing but the two exponents.","The larger constant, ka, goes on top of the ratio, and the difference goes underneath.","The logarithm of the ratio grows only slowly, while the difference grows quickly, so a drug absorbed far faster than it is eliminated peaks early, which is the ordinary case."]}]
